Subject: Materialises call arguments in place instead of staging copies

What this does
  Materialises call arguments in place instead of staging copies.

Why we need it
  Every register-VM call staged each argument into a window register with an explicit move, and for a freshly computed argument that move is the only reader of the value.

What it adds
  `regvm_arg_retarget` proves a value has no other reader and no window-naming instruction after its definition, `regvm_stage_args` applies that across one call's operand list and refuses a shared producer, and the six call lowerings retarget the producer instead of emitting a move.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
